#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-CG0521 expect=skipped domain=DM
#note "ARMCD column absent while ARM is populated. THE ALL-FACET GATE, NEW WITH D-16 (owner ruling 2026-09-12, executed 2026-09-13): the Check's bare empty(ARMCD) leaf would fire once per ARM-populated row under absent = all-missing, exactly as the L1-equivalent FDA/PMDA-SD1361 did before OR-wave 1 pinned them. Requirements.Variables.All [ARMCD, ARM] now rejects the dataset, SKIPPED naming the variable - ruling in documentation/derivation/absent-column-verdicts.tsv (verdict 2-2: the pair-consistency question is unanswerable without both columns; ARM/ARMCD are Expected in DM, so the absence is separately reported). Row 1 WOULD fire were the gate removed. If this scenario EXECUTES, the gate has been removed: escalate, do not rewrite the pin."
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-4
dataset DM class="SPECIAL PURPOSE" label="Demographics"
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN  type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col ARM     type=Char label="Description of Planned Arm"
---
S1 | DM | 001 | Treatment A
